  "edges": [
    {
      "id": "edge:containment:dyad_boundary",
      "attrs": {
        "i2t:category": "containment",
        "i2t:predicate": "contains",
        "i2t:evidence": "Every game operates on two distinct communicative levels simultaneously... within the interpersonal relation."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "edge:reference:overt_narrative_appeal",
      "attrs": {
        "i2t:category": "reference",
        "i2t:predicate": "appeals_to_prudence",
        "i2t:evidence": "The initiator presents a posture of delicate vulnerability: 'I have been wounded before; I move slowly and require complete emotional safety.' This overt message appeals directly to the cautious believer's self-image."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "edge:interactivity:covert_friction_deployment",
      "attrs": {
        "i2t:category": "interactivity",
        "i2t:predicate": "deploys_covert_test",
        "i2t:evidence": "Step 1: The Covert Test. The initiator introduces an ambiguous friction, an unspoken demand, or an emotional withdrawal, cloaked in the language of distress."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "edge:state_change:caution_to_rationalization",
      "attrs": {
        "i2t:category": "state_change",
        "i2t:predicate": "triggers_deliberation",
        "i2t:relation_to_canonical": "token-dag",
        "i2t:evidence": "The cautious believer interprets the initiator's hesitation or sudden withdrawal not as a covert test, but as a rational call for greater caution and deeper accommodation."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "edge:state_change:rationalization_to_concession",
      "attrs": {
        "i2t:category": "state_change",
        "i2t:predicate": "yields_boundary_ground",
        "i2t:relation_to_canonical": "token-dag",
        "i2t:evidence": "Step 2: The Cautious Accommodation. Believing that carefulness will de-escalate tension, the believer suppresses their own immediate reaction, rationalizes the initiator's behavior, and concedes ground."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "edge:state_change:concession_drives_goalpost_shift",
      "attrs": {
        "i2t:category": "state_change",
        "i2t:predicate": "validates_and_shifts",
        "i2t:relation_to_canonical": "token-dag",
        "i2t:evidence": "Step 3: The Shifting Baseline. The concession does not resolve the tension; instead, it validates the initiator's unconscious suspicion... The goalpost moves: the accommodation that was sufficient yesterday becomes the bare minimum today."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "edge:state_change:baseline_escalates_to_corner",
      "attrs": {
        "i2t:category": "state_change",
        "i2t:predicate": "enforces_corner",
        "i2t:relation_to_canonical": "token-dag",
        "i2t:evidence": "Step 4: The Double-Bind Corner. Eventually, the believer attempts to set a gentle, cautious boundary. The initiator immediately pivots: 'You claim to care, but your hesitation proves you are just like everyone else.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "edge:state_change:reinforcing_game_loop",
      "attrs": {
        "i2t:category": "state_change",
        "i2t:predicate": "restarts_insatiable_cycle",
        "i2t:relation_to_canonical": "type-quotient",
        "i2t:evidence": "The trap lies in this: the initiator's demand for reassurance is structurally insatiable because its root is an unconscious fear of exposure... tests must become harder to feel real."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "edge:interactivity:asymmetric_payoff_extraction",
      "attrs": {
        "i2t:category": "interactivity",
        "i2t:predicate": "extracts_psychological_payoff",
        "i2t:evidence": "The payoff of the game is psychological stabilization for the initiator at the expense of cognitive exhaustion for the believer."
      }
    }
  ],
